// Entertainment Lineup — Bob Anderson at top per Mike (2026-05-08).
const performers = [
  {
    name: "Scott Page",
    role: "Saxophonist &amp; Renowned Artist &mdash; Pink Floyd, Supertramp, Toto",
    img: "/images/event/scott-page.jpg",
    bio: "Scott Page is one of rock&rsquo;s most influential and revered musicians &mdash; a saxophonist and celebrated artist whose revolutionary sound and trailblazing creative instincts have helped shape some of the greatest tours and recordings in music history. He toured the world with <strong>Pink Floyd</strong> on the era-defining <em>A Momentary Lapse of Reason</em> and <em>Delicate Sound of Thunder</em> world tours, recorded and toured with <strong>Supertramp</strong> on <em>Brother Where You Bound</em>, and has brought his signature sound to <strong>Toto</strong> and a long list of rock&rsquo;s most celebrated acts.",
    bioExpanded: "<p>Scott Page&rsquo;s career has been one continuous arc through some of the most important moments in modern rock. As <strong>Pink Floyd</strong>&rsquo;s saxophonist on the <em>A Momentary Lapse of Reason</em> world tour (1987&ndash;1988) and the subsequent <em>Delicate Sound of Thunder</em> tour, he performed on some of the highest-grossing concerts of the era &mdash; his solos captured forever on the live recordings and films that defined a generation of arena rock.</p><p>His collaboration with <strong>Supertramp</strong> on the 1985 <em>Brother Where You Bound</em> album and the accompanying World Tour cemented his place among rock&rsquo;s most in-demand touring saxophonists. He has also brought his signature sound to <strong>Toto</strong> and a long list of legendary acts &mdash; the kind of breadth that makes him not just a great musician but a voice that has helped shape how a generation of rock and roll sounds.</p><p>Beyond music, Scott is a renowned artist and creative force whose work and instincts have reached far beyond the stage. From traditional visual art to the cutting edge of multimedia and digital experience, he has built a body of work that has inspired generations of musicians, artists, and creators &mdash; and put him at the front of many of the most important conversations in modern entertainment.</p><p>We are thrilled to welcome Scott Page to the Countdown 250 Ball. His musicianship, artistry, and unmistakable energy will help make America&rsquo;s 250th birthday celebration truly unforgettable.</p>",
  },
  {
    name: "Lee Greenwood",
    role: "All-American Icon Honoree &mdash; Performing &ldquo;God Bless the USA&rdquo;",
    img: "/images/event/lee-greenwood-hero.jpg",
    bio: "Lee Greenwood will be honored with the All-American Icon Award and take the stage for a special performance of his signature anthem, &ldquo;God Bless the USA&rdquo; &mdash; the song that has served as an unofficial anthem of American patriotism for more than four decades.",
    bioExpanded: "<p>A Grammy-winning singer-songwriter and member of the Grand Ole Opry, Greenwood released &ldquo;God Bless the USA&rdquo; in 1984. It became one of the most-played patriotic songs in American history &mdash; resurging powerfully after September 11, 2001 and remaining a defining sound of national pride at inaugurations, military ceremonies, and civic events across the country.</p><p>Over a career spanning more than four decades, he has performed for every U.S. President since Ronald Reagan and become one of the most visible champions of America&rsquo;s veterans and active military, recognized for a lifetime of service to military families.</p>",
  },
  {
    name: "Bob Anderson",
    role: "American Icon &amp; World&rsquo;s Greatest Singing Impressionist",
    img: "/images/event/bob-anderson.jpg",
    bio: "<em class='block mb-3 text-navy/80 not-italic font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider text-xs'>American Icon and the World&rsquo;s Greatest Singing Impressionist</em>Bob Anderson&rsquo;s career began with the kind of only-in-Las-Vegas moment that becomes legend. A Vietnam veteran from a musical family of six brothers known as &ldquo;The Detroit Osmonds,&rdquo; Anderson arrived in Las Vegas in his early twenties and, within hours, found himself on stage at the famed Sahara Hotel &amp; Casino. What began as an unexpected opportunity to sing with Nancy Sinatra quickly led to an appearance on The Merv Griffin Show, where his remarkable ability to recreate the voices of the world&rsquo;s greatest singers brought him national attention.<br /><a href='https://youtu.be/iGRT3H-XDkM' target='_blank' rel='noopener noreferrer' class='youtube-modal-trigger inline-flex items-center justify-center gap-2 mt-4 bg-navy-dark hover:bg-navy border-2 border-gold text-gold hover:text-gold-light px-4 sm:px-5 py-2.5 text-xs sm:text-sm font-bold uppercase tracking-wider transition-all rounded-lg shadow-md hover:shadow-lg hover:-translate-y-0.5 no-underline' data-yt-id='iGRT3H-XDkM' data-yt-title='Bob Anderson &mdash; &ldquo;The House I Live In&rdquo;'><span class='text-gold'>&#9654;</span> Listen to Bob Anderson&rsquo;s &ldquo;The House I Live In&rdquo;</a>",
    bioExpanded: "Over the next five decades, Anderson became one of the most sought-after entertainers on the Las Vegas Strip, performing in every major casino showroom and earning acclaim for his extraordinary recreations of legendary vocalists, including his celebrated tribute to Frank Sinatra. His career has included performances for two U.S. Presidents, the Royal Family, and audiences at Carnegie Hall, where his Sinatra performance earned multiple standing ovations.<br /><br />Inducted into both the Casino Legends Hall of Fame and the Las Vegas Entertainers Hall of Fame, Bob Anderson has been hailed by <em>People</em> Magazine as &ldquo;America&rsquo;s Greatest Singing Impressionist,&rdquo; praised by Simon Cowell as the best on the planet, and summed up best by Frank Sinatra himself: &ldquo;Bob Anderson has a hell of an act.&rdquo;",
  },
  {
    name: "Celeste Kellogg",
    role: "Country Music&rsquo;s Rising Star &mdash; Award-Winning Singer, Songwriter &amp; Actress",
    img: "/images/event/celeste-kellogg.jpg",
    bio: "Celeste Kellogg is one of country music&rsquo;s hottest rising stars &mdash; an award-winning, Nashville-based singer, songwriter, and actress whose powerful voice, magnetic stage presence, and heartfelt storytelling are captivating audiences across the country.",
    bioExpanded: "<p>Blending modern country with the energy of 90s and 2000s pop and the grit of 70s and 80s rock, Kellogg brings a fresh, dynamic sound to today&rsquo;s country music scene. Her singles &ldquo;Country Swagger&rdquo; and &ldquo;There&rsquo;s a Beach Somewhere&rdquo; have been featured on Spotify and CMT playlists and charted on the Music Row Country Airplay charts. She has also shared the stage with major artists including Miley Cyrus, Kelly Clarkson, and Brett Eldredge.</p><p>At the Countdown 250 Ball, Kellogg will bring her passion, patriotism, and unmistakable voice to America&rsquo;s most anticipated Independence Eve celebration. One of the evening&rsquo;s most meaningful musical moments will come when she performs her original patriotic anthem, &ldquo;Faith in Freedom&rdquo; &mdash; a powerful song inspired by her belief that America&rsquo;s strength is found in faith, freedom, courage, truth, and the willingness to love one another across our differences.<br /><a href='https://youtu.be/Z7GX-AVK11Y' target='_blank' rel='noopener noreferrer' class='youtube-modal-trigger inline-flex items-center justify-center gap-2 mt-4 bg-navy-dark hover:bg-navy border-2 border-gold text-gold hover:text-gold-light px-4 sm:px-5 py-2.5 text-xs sm:text-sm font-bold uppercase tracking-wider transition-all rounded-lg shadow-md hover:shadow-lg hover:-translate-y-0.5 no-underline' data-yt-id='Z7GX-AVK11Y' data-yt-title='Celeste Kellogg &mdash; &ldquo;Faith in Freedom&rdquo;'><span class='text-gold'>&#9654;</span> Listen to Celeste Kellogg&rsquo;s &ldquo;Faith in Freedom&rdquo;</a></p><p>With appearances across the country, a scheduled Main Stage performance at the Great American State Fair in Washington, D.C., and a growing reputation as one of country music&rsquo;s most exciting young voices, Celeste Kellogg is poised to deliver a performance worthy of America&rsquo;s historic 250th birthday celebration.</p>",
  },
  {
    name: "Gerardo Velez",
    role: "Renowned Percussionist &mdash; Jimi Hendrix, Spyro Gyra, 7&times; Grammy Nominee",
    img: "/images/event/gerardo-velez.jpg",
    bio: "Gerardo Velez is a master percussionist whose career has carried him through some of the most influential moments in modern music. He performed with <strong>Jimi Hendrix</strong> at Woodstock in 1969, became a founding rhythmic voice in the jazz-fusion ensemble <strong>Spyro Gyra</strong>, and has collaborated with legendary artists including <strong>David Bowie</strong>, <strong>Fleetwood Mac</strong>, and <strong>Nile Rodgers &amp; Chic</strong>. He is a seven-time Grammy nominee.",
    bioExpanded: "<p>Velez&rsquo;s instinct for rhythm has put him on stage and in studios with some of the most innovative musicians of the past five decades. His work with <strong>Jimi Hendrix</strong> &mdash; including his unforgettable performance at Woodstock as part of <strong>Gypsy Sun and Rainbows</strong> &mdash; placed him inside one of the defining sounds of the era. His role in shaping <strong>Spyro Gyra</strong>&rsquo;s groundbreaking sound helped define what jazz fusion could be.</p><p>From there, his collaborations have spanned rock, pop, soul, and world music &mdash; <strong>David Bowie</strong>, <strong>Fleetwood Mac</strong>, <strong>Nile Rodgers and Chic</strong>, and dozens more. Seven Grammy nominations across his career mark him as one of the world&rsquo;s most respected Latin rhythm percussionists.</p><p>At Countdown 250, he brings the same fire, precision, and joy that has earned him the respect of his peers across genres for generations.</p>",
  },
  {
    name: "The DC Transit Band",
    role: "Nine-Piece Powerhouse &mdash; Featuring a Once-in-a-Lifetime Jam with Rock Legends Scott Page &amp; Gerardo Velez",
    img: "/images/event/dc-transit-band.jpg",
    bio: "<em class='block mb-3 text-red-700 not-italic font-extrabold uppercase tracking-[0.3em] text-xs'>&#9733; Never-Before, Never-Again Jam &#9733;</em><strong class='text-navy text-base sm:text-lg block mb-3 leading-snug'>We are thrilled to add The DC Transit Band to the monumental Countdown 250 lineup.</strong>One of the most sought-after bands on the East Coast &mdash; a <strong>nine-piece powerhouse</strong> known for mesmerizing performances, huge audience energy, and the kind of crowd interaction that turns a dance floor into a full-on celebration. At Countdown 250, we&rsquo;re going even bigger: <strong>rock legends Scott Page</strong> (<strong>Pink Floyd</strong>, <strong>Supertramp</strong>, <strong>Toto</strong>) and <strong>Gerardo Velez</strong> (<strong>Jimi Hendrix</strong>, <strong>Spyro Gyra</strong>) <strong>will be joining the band on stage</strong> for an exclusive once-in-a-lifetime jam through some of America&rsquo;s greatest rock anthems.",
    bioExpanded: "<p>The DC Transit Band is a nine-piece powerhouse with a <strong>screamin&rsquo; three-piece horn section</strong>, a thumpin&rsquo; rhythm section, and <strong>two dynamic lead vocalists</strong> &mdash; the kind of full-band sound that has made them one of the most sought-after acts on the East Coast. Their setlist spans Top-40 hits, Classic Rock, R&amp;B, Funk, Disco, and Jazz Standards, and their performances are known for the kind of mesmerizing high-energy crowd interaction that keeps audiences on their feet from the first downbeat to the last encore.</p><p>At Countdown 250, the band is going somewhere they have never gone before. <strong>Scott Page</strong> &mdash; the legendary saxophonist behind <strong>Pink Floyd</strong>&rsquo;s <em>A Momentary Lapse of Reason</em> and <em>Delicate Sound of Thunder</em> world tours, and a sideman for <strong>Supertramp</strong> and <strong>Toto</strong> &mdash; will be joining The DC Transit Band on stage. So will <strong>Gerardo Velez</strong>, the master percussionist who performed alongside <strong>Jimi Hendrix</strong> at Woodstock and helped shape the groundbreaking sound of <strong>Spyro Gyra</strong>. Two musicians whose careers have helped shape the soundtrack of generations, dropping in with a nine-piece band built to make any room move.</p><p>Together, they&rsquo;ll tear into some of America&rsquo;s greatest rock anthems for a <strong class='text-red-700'>never-before, never-again</strong> jam session that exists only because America&rsquo;s 250th birthday brought them all into the same room at the same time. This is the kind of moment that makes the Countdown 250 Ball the celebration of a lifetime.</p><p>Learn more about the band at <a href='https://thedctransitband.com' target='_blank' rel='noopener noreferrer' class='text-red-700 font-semibold hover:text-red-900'>thedctransitband.com</a>.</p>",
  },
  {
    name: "MARCEY",
    role: "DJ &amp; Producer",
    img: "/images/event/dj-marcey.jpg",
    bio: "MARCEY is a Washington, D.C. based DJ and producer known for delivering high-energy sets that blend underground grit with mainstream appeal. He has established a strong presence in the D.C. dance music scene, performing at top venues including Echostage, The Anthem, Soundcheck, and Zebbie&rsquo;s Garden.",
    bioExpanded: "MARCEY has also supported major artists such as Martin Garrix, D.O.D, Ian Asher, and Matt Sassari &mdash; further solidifying his position as a rising act. With additional performances across the East Coast &mdash; including New York City, Tampa, and Fort Lauderdale &mdash; MARCEY continues to build momentum, driven by a passion to recreate the same energy and emotion that first drew him to dance music.<br /><br /><a href='https://www.instagram.com/marcey.mp3' target='_blank' rel='noopener noreferrer' class='inline-block text-red-700 font-bold uppercase tracking-wider text-xs hover:text-red-900'>Follow MARCEY on Instagram &rarr;</a>",
  },
  {
    name: "Julian Awari",
    role: "National Anthem",
    img: "/images/event/julian-awari.jpg",
    bio: "Air Force veteran and powerhouse vocalist. Performs the National Anthem to open the evening&rsquo;s program &mdash; a signature moment that sets the tone for the entire night.",
  },
  {
    name: "Deebo",
    role: "Rising-Star Open-Format DJ &middot; The Decades Dance Club",
    img: "/images/event/deebo.jpg",
    bio: "One of the East Coast&rsquo;s fastest-rising DJs, Deebo has a rare gift for getting every guest on the dance floor. He&rsquo;ll be rocking out at the <strong class='text-gold'>Decades Dance Club</strong> all night long with an incredible open-format mix of the biggest hits from the 80s, 90s, 2000s, and 2010s &mdash; four decades of American dance music, mixed nonstop.",
    bioExpanded: "<p>Deebo is a rising-star DJ known across the East Coast for one thing above all &mdash; <strong>packing the dance floor and keeping it packed all night</strong>. His superpower is reading a room in seconds and mixing the exact songs the crowd didn&rsquo;t know they needed. Every guest hears the song that made them fall in love with music, and every guest ends up on the floor.</p><p>At the Countdown 250 Ball, Deebo will be rocking out at the <strong>Decades Dance Club</strong> all night long. Expect a nonstop, decade-hopping open-format mix of the biggest hits from the <strong>80s, 90s, 2000s, and 2010s</strong> &mdash; MTV-era anthems, big-hair power ballads, Y2K club bangers, hip-hop classics, boy-band hooks, and 2010s dance-floor smashes, blended into one seamless celebration of four decades of American music.</p><p>Known for smooth transitions, creative mash-ups, and unmatched stage presence, Deebo started his DJ career in early college and has spent years building his name through relentless energy, consistency, and a gift for turning a room full of strangers into a crowd of best friends. If you&rsquo;re in the Decades Dance Club at Countdown 250, you will be dancing.</p>",
  },
  {
    name: "DJ JUMP",
    role: "Rising-Star Open-Format DJ &middot; The Magic Man of Music",
    img: "/images/event/dj-jump.jpg",
    bio: "We are thrilled to add DJ JUMP to the Countdown 250 Ball lineup. From his humble starts rocking the house at <strong>East Carolina University</strong>, DJ JUMP has grown throughout the East Coast and made a name for himself as <strong class='text-gold'>the Magic Man of Music</strong> &mdash; the guy who can read any room in seconds and turn every dance floor into an unforgettable celebration.",
    bioExpanded: "<p>DJ JUMP&rsquo;s rise is a classic East Coast success story. From his humble starts rocking the house at <strong>East Carolina University</strong>, he has built his name one gig at a time &mdash; college parties, packed club nights, private events, and major weekend celebrations up and down the East Coast &mdash; earning a reputation for one thing above all: knowing how to make a room lose control on the dance floor.</p><p>He&rsquo;s known throughout the region as <strong>the Magic Man of Music</strong>, a nickname earned through his gift for reading a crowd and blending genres, eras, and vibes into a nonstop journey that keeps every guest moving. From hip-hop to house, throwback anthems to today&rsquo;s biggest tracks, DJ JUMP&rsquo;s open-format sets are built around one goal: no one sits down.</p><p>We are thrilled to add DJ JUMP to the Countdown 250 Ball lineup. His unmatched energy, creativity, and gift for turning strangers into a dance-floor family will help make America&rsquo;s 250th birthday celebration one for the ages.</p>",
  },
  {
    name: "DJ Tharp",
    role: "High-Energy Dance Club DJ",
    img: "/images/misc/dj-cartoon.jpg",
